        "\n",
        "###  Introduction and Objectives\n",
        "The objective of this project is to design and evaluate a lightweight Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) constrained to under 100,000 trainable parameters. Our model is intended for deployment on a low resource edge device, specifically an **Automated Agricultural Sorting Machine** designed to classify 5 varieties of rice grains in real time.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "To emulate the memory and computational constraints of edge devices (such as microcontrollers), the input images are downscaled to a maximum resolution of `64x64` pixels.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Q8InwpaPrySL"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### 1. Data Preparation Strategy\n",
        "We utilized the **Rice Image Dataset**, which originally contains 75,000 images across 5 classes.\n",
        "To optimize training times and prevent Out Of Memory (OOM) failures typical in local environments, we randomly sub sampled exactly **2,000 images per class** (10,000 images total).\n",
        "\n",
        "To prevent data leakage and ensure balanced classes, we applied a strict **Stratified Train ,Validation ,Test Split**:\n",
        "* **Training Set:** 70% (7,000 images)\n",
        "* **Validation Set:** 15% (1,500 images)\n",
        "* **Testing Set:** 15% (1,500 images)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5HLU5ktjtJy6"
      }
    },
